WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.990
The creepy porcelain doll Annabelle is unleashed
again with a fresh set of spine-chilling demons

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.680
in Annabelle Comes Home.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.460
It's the third Annabelle movie and is actually
both a sequel and a prequel, and with Annabelle

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.180
having appeared in six out seven of the Conjuring
Universe's movies so far, things are getting

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.369
pretty complicated for the demonic doll's
timeline.

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:24.670
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining the full chronological

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.769
timeline for Annabelle in the Conjuring movie
franchise.

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:32.480
Plus I'll be discussing how the new movie
reveals a surprising connection to the Conjuring's

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.150
other big bad, the demon nun Valak.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:39.060
Spoilers ahead for Annabelle's appearances
in the Conjuring Universe movies.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.010
The timeline for Annabelle begins with Annabelle:
Creation which establishes the origins of

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.500
the demonic doll within the Conjuring universe.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.510
The movie begins in 1946 with doll maker Samuel
Mullins finishing his work on an exclusive

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.110
set of a hundred porcelain dolls.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:59.400
One day as the family returns from church,
their car breaks down and, while Samuel is

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.030
fixing it, the Mullins' daughter Annabelle,
also known as "Bee", is tragically killed

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.630
by a speeding car.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:10.290
You're going to want to remember Bee, because
she reappears many years later in Annabelle

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.290
Comes Home.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.420
"Can I play with Annabelle?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.250
I think you have the wrong house, there's
no Annabelle here.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.530
Yes she is."

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.030
After their daughter's death, the Mullins
are so devastated that they pray for a way

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.670
to see Bee again.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.420
They're contacted by a malevolent demon masquerading
as the spirit of their dead daughter who asks

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.870
for permission to move into one of Samuel's
porcelain dolls.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.270
A manifestation of Bee returns to the Mullins
household.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:39.890
However, when Esther realises it's not really
her daughter, the demon attacks her in an

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.310
attempt to take possession of her soul.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:46.450
The church steps in and manages to contain
the evil spirit in the doll.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:51.060
The doll is then sealed in Bee's closet which
is lined with pages from the holy Bible and

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.420
blessed by a priest for safety.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.690
This keeps the demon locked away until 1958
when the Mullins take Sister Charlotte and

00:01:58.690 --> 00:02:01.100
a group of orphans in to their home.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.880
One of the orphans, Janice, is mysteriously
lured into Bee's old bedroom where she finds

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.190
a key that opens Bee's closet.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.140
This releases the spirit of the Annabelle
demon which terrorises Janice and the other

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.170
girls over the following nights.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:18.760
By the way, similar events occur many years
later in Annabelle Comes Home when another

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.480
girl breaks the house rules, at the Warrens'
this time, when she finds a key and accidentally

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.590
releases the demon doll from the box which
is keeping her contained.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:32.010
Once Annabelle is unleashed in Annabelle:
Creation, we start to see her true demonic

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:35.580
form as the demon attempts to take Janice's
soul.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.550
"Will you help me?

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.520
What do you need?

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.000
Your soul!"

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.880
Janice escapes this encounter, but is disabled
further.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.990
And days later when she's taken outside, Annabelle
seems to summon another evil spirit of a nun

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:55.630
this time who pushes Janice into a barn so
that the demon in the form of Bee can attack

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.750
the young girl.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.250
Bee vomits into Janice's mouth, now possessing
her.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.780
The entity that helped Annabelle could very
well be the Conjuring's famous nun, Valak,

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:07.599
who starred in her own spin-off The Nun.

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:11.709
Annabelle's ability to call on other evil
spirits is revealed by Lorraine Warren in

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:12.770
Annabelle Comes Home.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:16.520
"It's the doll Ed, it's a beacon for other
spirits."

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:21.410
The Annabelle demon, who's now inside Janice,
begins a murderous rampage starting by killing

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:22.910
Samuel Mullins.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:27.739
And when Janice's friend realises what's going
on, she's tries to destroy the doll by throwing

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:28.870
it down the well.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:34.010
This fails, with the doll reappearing moments
later inside the farmhouse and it's the first

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:38.600
chronological example in the Conjuring Universe
of how it seems to be almost impossible to

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.840
destroy the doll once it's controlled by the
demon.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.800
In later films, Annabelle is dumped numerous
times in the trash, only to reappear later

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.489
back inside the building.

00:03:48.489 --> 00:03:53.100
In both The Conjuring and Annabelle Comes
Home, the Warrens explain that trying to destroy

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:57.680
the Annabelle doll "only makes things worse"
and that "the genie is better kept in the

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:58.780
bottle".

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.519
The only way to stop the Annabelle demon is
to contain it again.

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:07.489
In Annabelle: Creation, this only happens
when Sister Charlotte manages to shove Janice

00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:11.600
and the Annabelle doll into Bee's old closet,
jamming it shut.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.580
It's only a temporary measure though and when
the police come to investigate, they discover

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.469
that Janice has dug her way out through a
closet wall and escaped, leaving behind only

00:04:20.469 --> 00:04:24.340
the porcelain doll which is taken away by
the police.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.780
Janice ends up at another orphanage, and when
the Higgins family arrive to adopt her, she

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.089
reveals she now goes by the name of the demon
that's secretly hiding inside her.

00:04:33.089 --> 00:04:36.139
"I want to introduce you to Mr and Mrs Higgins.

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:37.919
"And you must be..."

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:38.919
"Annabelle."

00:04:38.919 --> 00:04:39.919
"Annabelle.

00:04:39.919 --> 00:04:41.740
What a lovely name."

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:47.020
Over the next 12 years, Annabelle Higgins,
aka Janice, grows up and joins a cult called

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.819
the Disciples of the Ram.

00:04:48.819 --> 00:04:54.029
The Annabelle doll then reappears in 1970
when John Form gives his wife Mia the doll

00:04:54.029 --> 00:04:55.360
to add to her collection.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.139
That same year, an adult Annabelle Higgins
returns to the home of her adoptive parents

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:03.099
and, together with her boyfriend, brutally
kills them.

00:05:03.099 --> 00:05:08.129
The crazed pair then break into Mia and John's
house next door, where Annabelle discovers

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:09.860
Mia's doll collection.

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:14.690
The possessed Annabelle Higgins tells Mia
"I like your dolls."

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:19.479
Which is echoed eerily later in Annabelle
Comes Home by the bloodied woman who suddenly

00:05:19.479 --> 00:05:24.059
appears to Lorraine inside the Warren's car
"I like your doll."

00:05:24.059 --> 00:05:28.009
During the Form's home invasion, Annabelle
kills herself while holding the porcelain

00:05:28.009 --> 00:05:31.449
doll and a trickle of her blood runs into
the doll's eye.

00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:35.900
This transfers the demon out of Annabelle's
human body back into the doll where it will

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.240
next begin to terrorise the Form family.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:44.080
After continued attacks by the doll, Mia and
John contact Father Perez who takes Annabelle

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.159
away to his church where he hopes the sacred
place will weaken the demon.

00:05:48.159 --> 00:05:53.259
The doll is able to conjure the form of Annabelle
Higgins who attacks the priest, and the Annabelle

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:59.139
doll ends up again in Mia's apartment to demand
her soul in return for sparing her baby.

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:04.129
To save Mia, her friend Evelyn sacrifices
her own soul by falling out of the window

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:06.349
together with the Annabelle doll.

00:06:06.349 --> 00:06:10.710
Moments later the doll disappears, reappearing
six months later in a store where a mother

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.789
buys it as a gift for her daughter, Debbie.

00:06:13.789 --> 00:06:18.300
This leads us into the prologue of The Conjuring
where Ed and Lorraine Warren investigate the

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.800
Annabelle case for the very first time.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.279
Debbie and her roommates explain to the Warrens
that their porcelain doll has been mysteriously

00:06:25.279 --> 00:06:27.229
moving around the apartment.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:32.069
To try and figure out what was going on, the
young nurses took it to a medium and the Annabelle

00:06:32.069 --> 00:06:36.240
demon then tricked them by pretending to be
the ghost of a 7-year-old girl called Annabelle

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.479
Higgins who'd died in the apartment.

00:06:38.479 --> 00:06:41.560
The demon said it wanted to be friends with
them as it was lonely.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.699
So the roommates gave it permission to move
into the doll at which point the demon started

00:06:45.699 --> 00:06:50.139
to terrorise them, damaging their belongings
and scrawling "miss me" all over the walls

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:55.249
and ceilings, and those messages reappear
later in Annabelle Comes Home.

00:06:55.249 --> 00:06:59.889
At this point, The Conjuring and Annabelle
Comes Home converge with the opening scene

00:06:59.889 --> 00:07:04.469
of Annabelle Comes Home reminding us how demonic
possession works within The Conjuring Universe:

00:07:04.469 --> 00:07:06.659
"It was a big mistake acknowledging this doll.

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.050
And through that, the inhuman spirit tricked
you.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:11.219
You gave it permission to infest your lives."

00:07:11.219 --> 00:07:13.199
"So the doll was never possessed?"

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:15.560
"No, no, it was used as a conduit.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.509
It was moved around to give the impression
of possession.

00:07:18.509 --> 00:07:20.509
Demonic spirits don't possess things.

00:07:20.509 --> 00:07:21.509
They possess people."

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:26.110
The Annabelle Comes Home prologue then fills
in a small narrative gap from The Conjuring

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:30.389
showing the Warrens telling the nurses they'll
take the Annabelle doll away to keep it somewhere

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:31.389
safe.

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:36.069
But before the doll reaches the relative security
of the Warren's artefact room, Ed and Lorraine

00:07:36.069 --> 00:07:40.960
have to drive it back home and the doll immediately
creates trouble causing their car to break

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.009
down outside a cemetery.

00:07:43.009 --> 00:07:47.800
While Ed is fixing the car, Annabelle summons
an array of spirits, one of which pushes Ed

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.289
into the path of an out-of-control truck,
in a call-back to how Bee was run over in

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:55.779
Annabelle Creation after the Higgins car broke
down.

00:07:55.779 --> 00:07:59.979
Ed and Lorraine do get the doll back to their
artefact room where they lock it away in a

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.689
cabinet made of church glass and have it blessed
by a priest.

00:08:03.689 --> 00:08:08.349
Like in Annabelle: Creation, this contains
the evil for now until the main events of

00:08:08.349 --> 00:08:11.909
Annabelle Comes Home which take place one
year later.

00:08:11.909 --> 00:08:17.229
Now, this is where the timeline gets a little
tricky because during this intervening year,

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:20.999
the main events of the first Conjuring movie
actually take place.

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:25.129
The Warren's investigation of the Perron haunting
in Harrisville, Rhodes Island takes place

00:08:25.129 --> 00:08:31.119
in 1971 and during that time the evil spirit
Bathsheba goes to the Warren's house and lets

00:08:31.119 --> 00:08:35.080
Annabelle loose and they both attack the Warren's
daughter Judy.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.000
By the way, if you're wondering why Judy looks
different in The Conjuring compared to Annabelle

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.660
Comes Home, it's because the producers decided
to recast Judy Warren with actress McKenna

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.680
Grace in the third Annabelle movie.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.690
So, after the Perron haunting in The Conjuring,
the main events of Annabelle Comes Home take

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:51.710
place.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:56.771
In this new Annabelle movie, babysitter Mary
Ellen's friend Daniela accidentally lets the

00:08:56.771 --> 00:09:01.311
Annabelle doll out of her glass cabinet after
touching pretty much everything in the Warren's

00:09:01.311 --> 00:09:02.440
artefact room.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:06.830
Annabelle, who as Lorraine explained is "a
beacon for other spirits", then unleashes

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:12.620
a horde of new demons and monsters on Judy,
Mary Ellen and Daniela who are home alone.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:16.640
In this movie, the Annabelle demon specifically
targets Judy and her soul, attacking the Warren's

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.640
daughter in various ways.

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:21.460
First Annabelle manifests as Bee, the Mullins'
daughter from Annabelle: Creation.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:25.820
She then also appears as Annabelle Higgins
from the first Annabelle movie, before emerging

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.520
as the demon itself.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:31.950
When Judy attempts to return the Annabelle
doll to the glass cabinet, the demon starts

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.090
to suck her soul from her body.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:38.450
Judy manages to grab a crucifix and place
it on the demon's head which weakens it until

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:43.030
all three girls are able to lock the Annabelle
doll back in the glass cabinet.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:47.650
At this point, all of the other demonic entities
that Annabelle summoned disappear.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:52.040
Shortly after Annabelle Comes Home on the
Conjuring timeline is The Curse of La Llorona

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.750
which takes place in 1973.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:59.300
The Annabelle doll appears in flashback when
Father Perez mentions his encounter with the

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.790
demon after Anna comes to him for help on
how to deal with the Weeping Woman.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:08.140
And Annabelle appears briefly at the very
end of The Conjuring 2 when Ed Warren puts

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:12.210
the Crooked Man zoetrope on the shelf near
the doll in the artefact room.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.760
The Crooked Man has a spin-off movie in development
which has been delayed due to the popularity

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.230
of The Nun, so it will be interesting to see
if Annabelle factors into that future story

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:22.660
in any way.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.610
Any of these new villains from Annabelle Comes
Home could return in the next Conjuring movie

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:32.020
or their own spin-offs, and it's been rumoured
that The Conjuring 3 may include demonic werewolves

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:36.420
which means we could see the Black Shuck from
Annabelle Comes Home return very soon.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:41.470
So, would you like to see any of the new demons
in Annabelle Comes Home get their own movie?

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.640
And do you think Annabelle should return in
the Conjuring Universe?

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.110
Let me know in the comments below.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:51.920
Next tap left to find out all about the deleted
ending to The Nun that you never got to see,

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.580
or tap right for another video you're sure
to like.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.580
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.690
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

